author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Help and contracts disclose policy plus change input; advertised example executes on an isolated nonempty tracker; missing policy returns precise executable recovery; original runtime and token ceilings are preserved
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make the documented risk command executable using only its declared help
value: Self-improvement risk selection can run without inspecting source for omitted prerequisites
why_now: The current help example reproducibly refuses because definition.policy is absent
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Make risk help and runtime contracts declare explicit policy and change, and return required-input context plus executable help recovery when policy is missing; record the production escape and strengthened gate before closure."
expected_result: "The advertised risk example executes, missing policy names its prerequisite, and terminal defect classification and gate evidence pass without fabricated project policy or weaker recurrence gates."
actual_result: Linked source SDK and real CLI tests pass against isolated nonempty trackers; exact complete-source coverage and unchanged grammar/recovery/token gates pass. The prior closure is preserved and the replacement closure includes accountable production-defect gate evidence. The empty-family example remains documented as request-shape guidance.
